    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d572">

                <pb facs="0627" n="617" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg617"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/8–2044:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-08-20T00:00:00+02:00">August 20,
                            1944—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received August 20—9:06 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6753. British have instructed Mallet to proceed with joint formal statement and
                    accompanying oral comments in accordance with Department’s 6607, August 19, 6
                    p.m. (1656 to Stockholm) as modified by Department’s 6614, August 19, 10 p.m.
                    (1659 to Stockholm), unless in the opinion of the British, Russian and American
                    Ministers the making of this approach on Monday, August 21, would jeopardize
                    Swedish Government ratification of the decision taken by Boheman on August 18 to
                    withdraw insurance from Swedish ships sailing to Baltic ports as reported in
                    Stockholm’s 3163, August 18.<anchor n="46" xml:id="d572-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent to Stockholm as 352 and repeated to Department as 6753 and Moscow as 90.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
